### Final commit
- bd12506 Add Hermes support with playable browser game and verified deployment (branch opencode/34309727151, pushed)

### Deployment status
- Local app server: tmux session app-server, python3 http.server on port 3000 serving repo root; GET /index.html and /dist/index.html both 200
- Public deployment: trycloudflare tunnel above returns 200 with the game page; rAF loop, keyboard input, HUD all live

### Test status
- Public browser check (tools/hermes/browser-public.js vs public URL): PASS — ticks advance (tick 25), HUD live, ArrowRight moves player x 8 to 19, zero page errors
- Local browser smoke (tools/hermes/browser-smoke.js): PASS
- Unit suite npm test: 17/17 PASS (compat 5, game determinism 6, build-verify 6)
- Hermes pipeline: compat exit 0 clean; build emits real .hbc under Hermes CLI (magic 0x1F1903C103BC1FC6, HBC v96, engine 0.12.0) and exit-4 fallback manifest otherwise; verify confirms header via hbcdump; run executes deterministically in hermes and node modes

### Known limitations
- dist/game.hbc is gitignored-by-omission here (only bundle + fallback manifest committed); rebuild bytecode with hermes:build wherever the Hermes CLI is installed
- Bytecode is engine-coupled: after any Hermes upgrade, bump engineVersion/bytecodeTarget together with a rebuilt .hbc (see docs/HERMES.md section 7)
- Config paths are trusted-local (no containment check); browser smoke needs system Chrome plus puppeteer-core (devDependency install required)" 2>&1 | tail -n 3
